WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.470
When it debuts on May 3rd, 2019, the fourth
Avengers movie will be tasked with accomplishing

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:10.640
an unprecedented feat in cinematic storytelling,
tying up one of the most sprawling sagas in

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.460
movie history.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.600
But all signs point to one certainty it will
pull it off in style.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.420
Tony's last stand

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.039
Considering the end credits scene of Infinity
War, a lot of speculation over the pending

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.340
defeat of the Mad Titan Thanos has centered
on the spacefaring Captain Marvel, Carol Danvers.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.440
But comments made by the directing team of
the Russo brothers have heavily implied that

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.200
the good Captain won't necessarily be a magic
bullet.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.480
The biggest threat to Thanos may be none other
than Iron Man.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.260
As Infinity War detailed, Thanos and Tony
are on a first-name basis, with both of them

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.120
holding deep-seated grudges over the first
Avengers' Battle of New York.

00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:50.559
While Captain Marvel's power level will surely
play a part in Thanos' defeat, it makes more

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:55.249
sense that Stark who kicked off the entire
MCU will be forced into a final showdown with

00:00:55.249 --> 00:00:55.840
Thanos.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.219
One way or another, it's probably the last
time we'll see Robert Downey Jr. in the role

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.400
but does the encounter have to end with his
death?

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.360
It's never been more plausible.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.620
Expiring contracts

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.080
Not only would a clash between Iron Man and
Thanos in which Stark meets his demise make

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.780
narrative sense, it would also make business
sense.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.210
Robert Downey Jr.'s contract with Marvel will
be completed with Avengers 4 and he's not

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.580
the only one whose time is up.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.620
While everyone who was snapped away in Infinity
War is probably coming back, the fates of

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:27.180
the original team members are much more up
in the air.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.850
We know that Avengers 4 will also complete
the contracts of Chris Evans, Chris Hemsworth,

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:32.920
and Jeremy Renner.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.580
The status of Mark Ruffalo's deal is unknown,
and though Scarlett Johansson is on board

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:41.480
for a Black Widow solo feature, there's no
guarantee that that film will take place in

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.220
the post-Avengers 4 timeline, meaning she
could be done for as well.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.660
There's a reason the original crew survived
Thanos' big Snappening for the old-school

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:52.600
members of the team, Avengers 4 is one last
ride.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.540
End of the Guardians?

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.360
The Guardians of the Galaxy series quickly
became one of the MCU's most cherished series

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.340
thanks to its adventurous tone and characters
that are outlandish, yet relatable.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.540
Their crossover with the Avengers in Infinity
War was long-awaited, and even though they

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:12.010
mostly turned to dust by the end of that film,
Dave Bautista has confirmed the team will

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.420
appear in Avengers 4.

00:02:13.829 --> 00:02:17.980
However, Disney's firing of writer-director
James Gunn and subsequent decision to put

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:22.659
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3 on hold has
thrown the entire future of the team into

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.160
question.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.540
And it's even been speculated that Avengers
4 may be reworked during reshoots to phase

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.500
out Gunn's version of the team permanently.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.680
For all we know, Avengers 4 will be the last
time we see the Guardians something that used

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.780
to seem unthinkable.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.340
Returning favorites

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.360
Infinity War saw many of our heroes being
reduced to dust, but the fates of more than

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.540
a few popular characters remained up in the
air.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.770
Luckily, many of their actors involved with
the movie seem to have difficulty keeping

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:53.940
their mouths shut, cluing us in to a few significant
characters who survived Thanos' snap.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.580
In an interview with ScreenRant during the
promotion cycle for Mission: Impossible Fallout,

00:02:58.599 --> 00:03:03.279
Angela Bassett let slip that not only did
her character Ramonda survive, so did her

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.780
genius daughter Shuri.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.390
Could she take up the mantle of Black Panther
while her brother is away?

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:12.849
Instagram detectives were also able to all
but confirm that Tessa Thompson's Valkyrie

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:15.660
will also be back after sitting out Infinity
War.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.900
But no sleuthing was required to determine
the fate of Wong, the trusted companion of

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:20.860
Doctor Strange.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:25.140
The character's actor, Benedict Wong, just
went ahead and posted a photo of himself on

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:25.640
set.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.860
His return will be welcomed, but that skull-peeling
photo has prompted wild speculation from fans

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:35.660
that Wong just might turn out be a Skrull
one of the shape-shifting alien baddies we'll

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.660
be introduced to in Captain Marvel.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.680
A cosmic culmination

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:44.440
Infinity War took the saga of the Avengers
to new heights, dramatically raising the stakes

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.640
of the conflict with Thanos by having the
Mad Titan actually succeed in his genocidal

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.140
mission.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.180
But Avengers 4 will give us something that
the Marvel Cinematic Universe hasn't had to

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.320
face until now: a conclusion.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:04:02.140
According to Marvel Studios mastermind Kevin
Feige, Avengers 4 the 22nd entry in the MCU

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:07.189
will completely wrap up the ten years' worth
of story that started unfolding with 2008's

00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:07.740
Iron Man.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:12.560
He acknowledged that the individual movies
within the MCU are perpetually in motion,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.100
always leaving viewers on the hook for a sequel
of some sort.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.120
This time, he says, will be refreshingly different.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.080
"We're in the endgame now."

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.840
Uncharted territory

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:28.540
Seasoned fans of the MCU know that the studio
has never directly adapted a story from the

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.180
comics, but rather used Marvel's decades of
print storylines for inspiration.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.710
The most obvious example of this is Captain
America: Civil War, which took its title from

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.700
a famous story arc while sharing only a few
basic plot points with its namesake.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:45.540
Infinity War is a loose adaptation of the
comics' Infinity Gauntlet story, but Marvel

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:51.140
isn't dipping into its back catalog for Avengers
4 according to directors Joe and Anthony Russo,

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.000
it will be a totally original story.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.060
Joe Russo told ComicBook.com,

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.560
"I have no interest as a director in telling
a story that's already been told or in seeing

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.820
one that's already been told.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.690
If I know all the events of the story as they're
going to happen, then what's the point of

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.500
going to the film?"

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:10.320
It's a good point, and one which means that
fans looking to Marvel comics for clues to

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.340
the conflict's outcome probably aren't going
to find them.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.580
Comic readers saw Thanos' snap coming from
miles away, but what comes after?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.100
Nobody knows.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.000
Thor speaks

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.350
If you're looking for general reassurance
that Avengers 4 will blow your mind just as

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:29.760
hard as Infinity War, look no further than
the words of the Odinson himself,

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:30.560
Chris Hemsworth.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.000
Speaking in an interview with Esquire, the
actor revealed his opinion that Avengers 4

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.240
will outdo its predecessor when it comes to
unexpected surprises, saying,

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.180
"If you were shocked by [Infinity War], I
think the second one is even more shocking,

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.400
for other reasons entirely.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.480
[…] The second one I'm probably even more
excited about."

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.580
While we're curious about where the story
will go, assurances like this are almost as

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.080
good.

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:56.320
Whatever happens, we're happy to let the wild
speculation continue until the movie's release.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.420
At least, until Mark Ruffalo comes around
and spoils the entire thing for us.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.760
"Wait til ya see this next one easy Mark everybody
dies."

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:04.900
"D-Dude!

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.120
Dude..." "... ...not everybody."

